{"name":"Weathered Plastic","hex":"#f9f4d9","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"weathered","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Worn by weather, as of rocks, stone, etc.","Made slightly sloping, so as to throw off water."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["simple past and past participle of weather"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/weathered"},{"term":"plastic","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A synthetic, solid, hydrocarbon-based polymer, whether thermoplastic or thermosetting.","Credit or debit cards used in place of cash to buy goods and services."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Capable of being moulded; malleable, flexible, pliant. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","Producing tissue."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/plastic"}],"entries":[{"title":"Weathered","blocks":[{"text":"Weathered is the third studio album by American rock band Creed, released on November 20, 2001. It was the last Creed album to be released until Full Circle in October 2009, as Creed disbanded in June 2004. Weathered is the only Creed album to be recorded as a trio, as bassist Brian Marshall departed in August 2000, with guitarist Mark Tremonti taking over the bass guitar part during recording. Tremonti and vocalist Scott Stapp wrote most of the material for the album during a three-week period in late 2000, following their successful tour to support their second album, Human Clay. Manager Jeff Hanson once again paired the band with long-time producer John Kurzweg, who rented out a private residence/recording studio in Ocoee, Florida owned by Jay Stanley, where the band set up a studio inside to record the album. Recording sessions for the album began in July 2001 and took four months to complete."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/a/a2/Weathered_Main_Cover.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Weathered","wikidata":"Q2321182"},{"title":"Plastic","blocks":[{"text":"Plastics are a wide range of synthetic or semisynthetic materials composed primarily of polymers. Their defining characteristic, plasticity, allows them to be molded, extruded, or pressed into a diverse range of solid forms. This adaptability, combined with a wide range of other properties such as low weight, durability, flexibility, chemical resistance, low toxicity, and low-cost production, has led to their widespread use around the world. While most plastics are produced from natural gas and petroleum, a growing minority are produced from renewable resources like polylactic acid."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b2/Plastic_household_items.jpg/330px-Plastic_household_items.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Plastic","wikidata":"Q11474"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/8/81/Weathered_Alternate_Cover.jpg/250px-Weathered_Alternate_Cover.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/8/81/Weathered_Alternate_Cover.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/8/81/Weathered_Alternate_Cover.jpg/250px-Weathered_Alternate_Cover.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Alternate cover artwork for Weathered with the enlarged solid white wordmark and album title, and Mark Tremonti's head carved facing to the right.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AWeathered_Alternate_Cover.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9c/Melted_plastic.jpg/330px-Melted_plastic.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9c/Melted_plastic.j